# Operating Mode — Solo vs Team

**Canonical rule**: `../../.claude/rules/solo-vs-team-mode.md` — full definition, examples, and transition process.

## Source of truth

Read `.claude/stack-*.yml` → `framework.mode` in the project workspace root. That field is authoritative; the root `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md` mention is informational.

Default when neither is declared: **team mode** (safer — more checkpoints, less accidental autonomy).

## Solo mode

When `framework.mode: solo`:

- **Run autonomously.** Don't wait for per-action human approval.
- **Move tickets through the pipeline.** AI may self-promote into AI-active columns (🤖 FRD Tech Plan, 💻 AI Development, 🧪 Staging Ready, 🔄 Rework) and out of them.
- **Merge to release branches** without per-merge human approval.
- **Log every autonomous move** as a ticket comment:

  ```
  Moved to <column> under solo mode on <YYYY-MM-DD>.
  ```

## Team mode

When `framework.mode: team`:

- **Strict ownership chain.** AI waits for human moves into AI-active columns.
- AI never self-promotes into `🤖 FRD Tech Plan`, `💻 AI Development`, `🧪 Staging Ready`, or `🔄 Rework`.
- Every column transition is a coordination point.
- Backlog → FRD Draft is triage lead's responsibility.
- PR review approval and Staging Review are human actions.

## Hard rules (apply in every mode)

- **Verification Gate** — every handoff to a review column needs pasted command output proving the change works.
- **Size Audit** — pre-work file measurement + auto tech-debt tickets.
- **Scope-discrepancy escalation** — pause and surface at 2× complexity budget.
- **Never merge to `master` / `main` / `dev`** — release branches only.
- **✅ Done is human-only** — AI never moves a ticket to Done.
- **Hard stops require chat confirmation**, even in solo mode:
  - Destructive ops: `rm -rf`, `drop table`, `reset --hard`, force push.
  - Financial actions.
  - Auth / permissions / secrets changes.
  - Anything listed under `prohibited_actions` in the canonical rule.

## Per-session override

Even in team mode, the human can grant a one-session autonomous override ("go autonomous on this batch"). Solo mode is effectively a permanent version of that, declared at the project level.
